      stub entry, stop (COUNT_LIST_MISMATCH). Only then is Voynich text read;
  (e) gates G1b then G1a; (f) real score; (g) CALL.
  Any gate failure in (b) (gate F0), (d0), (d1) or (d) stops s128. The report-only F0-N2 N60/N90 arms in (b) are not a gate: a miss
  on them is printed and does not stop s128.
  FILING (lead rule): whatever s128 ends in, a STOP at any gate or a CALL, it is filed and reported as the s128 result, as printed
  (runs/s128/results_s128_*.txt). A fix needs a new run id; a new run id never replaces, withdraws or overrides a filed s128 result,
  and any successor must cite s128 and its filed STOP or CALL.

QUESTION
Do Voynich herbal pages carry, as a real Circa Instans-type herbal does, a word type that is confined to one page, recurs on that page,
and first appears in the page's first line, beyond what the rarity and positional habits of paragraph-initial words (L-069, F-02) produce?

DATA (paths relative to the project root; sha256 in the stub; the scorer refuses to run if any hash differs)
- Primary: data/ZL3b-n.txt (ZL3b, IVTFF). Secondary: data/external/voynich-nu-ivtff/RF1b-er.txt, data/external/voynich-nu-ivtff/IT2a-n.txt.
- Page header variables are read with vparse.PAGE_RE / vparse.VAR_RE (vparse.py, hashed): $I illustration, $Q quire, $B bifolio within
  quire, $H hand, $L Currier language.
- Herbal page set: every page whose header has $I=H, minus the excluded foldouts.
- Excluded foldouts: every page id matching ^f[0-9]+[rv][0-9]+$ (multi-panel). The expected herbal panels under this rule are frozen in
  runs/s128/s128_excluded_foldouts.txt (f90r1 f90r2 f90v1 f90v2 f95r1 f95r2 f95v1 f95v2, taken from the published catalogue, not from a
  transliteration). The scorer prints every page it excludes; an excluded herbal page not on the list is printed as LIST_MISMATCH and is
  still excluded (the rule binds, the list is the audit).
- Sheet rule (written out; same as p1_bifolio_null.bifolio_of_pages, hashed): sheet = the pair ($Q, $B) from the page header.
  A page with $Q or $B missing has sheet '?' and forms its own sheet.

MARKUP-READING RULES (IVTFF; applied identically to all three files)
- File lines starting with '#' and blank lines are skipped.
- Page header: a line matching vparse.PAGE_RE '^<(f\w+)>\s+<!(.*)>'; header variables apply to the following text lines until the next header.
- Text line: a line matching vparse.LINE_RE '^<(f\w+)\.(\d+),(.)(\w+)>\s+(.*)$' -> page, line number, locus indicator (one character),
  unit code, text. One text line = one line for every s128 purpose.
- Locus indicator '!' (text that does not exist in the MS, IVTFF spec 6.4 Table 8): the line is excluded. No other locus indicator
  ('@', '+', '*', '=', ...) changes inclusion or paragraph structure; in particular '@' is NOT a paragraph start.
- Included units: unit codes P0, P1, Pb, Pc, Pr (running paragraph text). Excluded: Pt (titles), every L* (labels), C* (circular),
  R* (radial), S* and any other code. The scorer prints counts of unit codes seen on herbal pages and of lines excluded.
- Line order: file order within a page. Line 1 of a page = the first included text line of that page.
- Inline comments <!...> are removed. The drawing-interruption mark <-> is a word break inside the same line.
  Paragraph markers <%> (start) and <$> (end) are read for paragraph boundaries (below) and then removed; any other <...> tag is removed.
- Alternative readings [a:b] (or [a:b:c]) take the first reading. Ligature braces { } are removed, keeping the glyphs inside.
  Apostrophes and the filler characters '!' and '%' outside tags are removed.
- Word breaks: '.' (space) and ',' (uncertain space) both break words (vparse.clean default, strict_spaces=False).
- Uncertain glyphs: '?' (unreadable glyph), '*' (unreadable, older files) and @nnn; (rare-glyph code, mapped to '?' by vparse.clean)
  make the whole token uncertain. Uncertain tokens are deleted before any count; the positions of the remaining tokens close up within
  the line. A line left with zero tokens is dropped (the next included line becomes line 1 if it was line 1).
- Paragraph start: (i) the first kept line of a page; (ii) any kept line whose text, after removing inline comments, begins with <%>;
  (iii) the kept line after a line whose text, after removing inline comments, ends with <$>. A <%> or a <$> on a line dropped as
  empty carries to the next kept line of the same page (it flags that line as a paragraph start). "Kept" = included and not empty
  after token deletion.
- If ZL3b has no <%> mark on any included herbal line, the primary STOPS (STOP_NO_PARA_MARKS); there is no fallback for the primary.
  For RF1b and IT2a only, if a file has no <%> mark, a LAYOUT_PROXY is used, report-only: paragraph starts by rules (i) and (iii) only;
  every result from it is labelled LAYOUT_PROXY and enters no call.
- Slots: paragraph-initial = first token of a paragraph-start line; line-initial = first token of any other included line; other = the rest.

UNITS
- Primary: whole words. Secondary (report only): cores under scoreboard/metrics_new.py SlotSegmenter and under
  s76_segmenter_independence.py ZatteraSegmenter("drop", "primary") (both hashed; X-01 at risk).

STATISTIC S (adapted from the calibration definition: the reference corpus is now per Currier language)
- Reference corpus: all herbal pages of the same Currier language as the page ($L; pages with no $L form their own reference group '?',
  printed with its page count).
- Page-confined recurring type on page p: count on p >= 2 and count on p / count in the reference corpus >= 0.9.
- Per page: if it has at least one such type, take the one whose first occurrence on p is earliest; hit = that occurrence is in line 1.
- S = hits / number of pages in the s128 page set.
- s128 PAGE SET (one set everywhere: count list, S, N1, N2, F0-N2-REAL, G1b, G1a, LOQO): herbal pages, foldouts excluded, with at
  least one kept line. A herbal page with no kept line (e.g. labels only, or every token uncertain) is listed with its count in the
  count-list header (#herbal_pages_no_kept_line), printed by the scorer, and left out of the count list and of S's denominator.
- Primary: ZL3b, whole words, pooled herbal. Also reported: Herbal A only, Herbal B only.

NULLS (S recomputed on each draw with the reference counts of the permuted corpus; p = (1 + #draws >= obs) / (draws + 1);
q99 = the 99th percentile, i.e. sorted draw index ceil(0.99 * draws) - 1)
- N2 (DECISIVE), 1,000 draws, seed 20261019. Stratum = (quire $Q, sheet ($Q,$B), hand $H, Currier language $L): where a sheet mixes hands
  or languages, swaps happen only between its pages sharing both. Paragraph-initial tokens are permuted among the paragraph-initial
  slots of all pages in the stratum. Line-initial tokens are permuted among the line-initial slots of the same page. Other tokens are
  permuted among the other slots of the same page. Line lengths and paragraph structure are kept.
  Single-page widening: if the pages that are alone in their ($Q, sheet, $H, $L) stratum are more than 25% of the pages of the s128
  page set (pages held in place, below, count in that denominator, not in the numerator), those single pages only are re-stratified
  by (quire, hand, language) among themselves: a widened page joins only other widened pages with the same ($Q, $H, $L) and never
  merges into an existing multi-page stratum with the same ($Q, $H, $L). A page still alone after widening, or alone when the 25% line
  is not crossed, is a one-page stratum: its paragraph-initial tokens are permuted only among its own paragraph-initial slots (a page
  with one paragraph start keeps its start token in place). The scorer prints the number of widened pages and of one-page strata.
  Pages with no $H or no $L value ('?' from vparse) are left out of the N2 strata: their paragraph-initial tokens are not swapped
  with any other page (held in place), while their line-initial and other tokens are permuted within the page as above. They stay in
  S and in N1. The count of such pages is printed.
- N1 (NON-DECISIVE, always reported beside N2), 1,000 draws, seed 20261020: all tokens of a page permuted within the page, line lengths kept.

COUNT LIST (step d0; the only Voynich-file access before step d)
- Script: runs/s128/s128_layout_counts_v2.py (sha256 in the stub; frozen now; never run on a Voynich file before HOLD 1 clears).
  It checks its own, vparse.py's and the data file's sha256 against the stub before opening the data file (exit 2 on mismatch),
  then imports vparse.py and applies exactly the page-set, unit, locator, paragraph and tokenising rules above.
- Output runs/s128/s128_layout_counts_ZL3b.tsv, ASCII, LF. Header lines: script tag, source path, source file sha256, number of <%>
  marks on included herbal lines, excluded foldout pages (count and ids), herbal pages with no kept line (count and ids).
  Then one row per page of the s128 page set in file order:
  page id, $Q, $B, $H, $L, comma-separated token count of each kept line in order, comma-separated paragraph-start flag (1/0) per line.
  No word content, glyph or token string is written or printed.
- Its sha256 is appended to the stub before F0-N2-REAL runs. At step (d) the scorer rebuilds the file byte for byte; a different
  sha256 stops s128 (COUNT_LIST_MISMATCH).
- Development checks done before freezing (no Voynich data), all in runs/s128/s128_v4_fixture/ (counts_tests.log, f0n2_tests.log, inputs, outputs, test stubs):
  C1 hand-written IVTFF fixture -> exit 0, incl. a <%> on a line dropped as empty carried to the next kept line, '@' mid-page not a
  start, a herbal page with labels only listed under #herbal_pages_no_kept_line; C2 data hash mismatch, C3 own hash mismatch,
  C4 vparse.py altered, C5 data file not in stub -> each exit 2 with nothing written; C6 no <%> marks -> exit 3 (a file written
  on exit 3 is never hashed into the stub or used).

GATES BEFORE ANY VOYNICH TEXT IS READ (F0 and the N60/N90 arms: calibration texts only; F0-N2-REAL: calibration texts + count list)
- F0 scorer fixture, seeds 20261021..20261030 (10). On the calibration Egerton set at start_N90 (each chapter cut to its first 90
  tokens: calibration file line 9, made by runs/s128/s128_herbal_profile.py analyse(N=90, window='start'), lines 104-106 and 234-235;
  8-token pseudo-lines, one paragraph per chapter, reference corpus = all chapters): the scorer reproduces S = 0.266 +/- 0.01 (S does
  not depend on the seed) and, with 200 N1 draws per seed, N1 q99 = 0.134 +/- 0.02 (calibration file line 9) in >= 9 of the 10 seeds;
  every seed's N1 q99 is printed.
  With tokens shuffled within chapter (one shuffle per seed), S is not above its N1 q99 (200 draws) in >= 9 of 10 seeds.
- F0-N2 N60/N90 arms (REPORT-ONLY), seeds 20261031..20261045 (15). Per seed: draw 28 random blocks of 4 consecutive
  Egerton chapters (112 pages, about the herbal page count); pseudo-stratum = the block of 4 (a sheet stand-in, one hand, one language);
  pages truncated to N = 60 and N = 90 tokens; 8-token pseudo-lines; one paragraph per page (paragraph-initial = token 0, where Egerton
  places the name 86% of the time, calibration file line 9); N2 and N1 with 200 draws each.
  Arm NAME (real Egerton, name in the paragraph-initial slot): expected S > N2 q99 in >= 10/15 seeds at both N.
  Arm RARITY (every name-stem token replaced by the common word 'et'; token 0 replaced by a fresh type that occurs nowhere else):
  expected S > N2 q99 in <= 5/15 seeds at both N. (Limit noted by the Verifier: this arm shows N2 does not invent hits; it does not
  separate a rarity-only start from a name.)
  Frozen expected outcome (already observed in runs/s128/results_s128_f0n2_calibration.txt with s128_f0n2_calib.py): NAME 15/15 at
  N60 and N90 (median S 0.339 / 0.384, N2 q99 0.250 / 0.259); RARITY 1/15 and 0/15 (median S 0.098 / 0.107, N2 q99 0.170 / 0.179).
  These N60/N90 arms are REPORT-ONLY in v5, this prereg (Verifier N2 ruling); they do not decide, and a miss does not stop s128.

- F0-N2-REAL, the DECIDING known-answer check for N2 (step d1; after the count list exists, before any Voynich text is read).
  Code: runs/s128/s128_f0n2_real.py only (hash in the stub now, before the count list exists). Inputs: the count list
  runs/s128/s128_layout_counts_ZL3b.tsv (hash appended at d0) and the Egerton chapters of the calibration set (Ventura TEI, edition
  order, parsed with the rules of runs/s128/s128_herbal_profile.py load_egerton). Seeds 20261046..20261060 (15), one per replicate;
  each seed's random.Random(seed) gives the start chapter and then all N2 and N1 draws of that seed.
  Mapping, per seed:
  - Pages are taken in count-list order and grouped into their N2 strata exactly as in N2 (same keys, same single-page widening,
    same hold-in-place rule for pages with no $H or $L).
  - rng = random.Random(seed); start = rng.randrange(number of Egerton chapters). Chapters are consumed in edition order from start,
    wrapping round, each at most once per seed; strata are filled in order of their first page in the count list, so each stratum
    gets a block of consecutive chapters. Within a stratum, pages are filled in count-list order. Pages held in place (no $H or $L)
    are filled after all strata, in count-list order.
  - Each chapter is poured into one page: its tokens in order fill line 1 to that line's real token count, then line 2, and so on.
    Tokens past the page's last slot are dropped (the page keeps exactly its count-list size).
    Paragraph-start flags and slot classes come from the count list; the chapter's token 0 is therefore the paragraph-initial token
    of line 1 (where Egerton places the name 86% of the time).
  - Too short: a chapter with fewer tokens than the page's total is skipped (counted SHORT_SKIP) and the next chapter is used. If more
    than 50% of the chapters examined in a seed are skipped, or the edition runs out before every page is filled, the seed FAILS.
    (v4 change from 10%: on a made-up count list with Voynich-like sizes, 4-10 tokens x 5-12 lines, the skip rate was 13-31% in every
    seed, because a quarter of Egerton chapters have fewer than 70 tokens; a 10% cap would fail the gate for chapter length alone.)
  - A FAILED seed counts as a NAME miss and as a RARITY fire (the conservative reading for both arms).
  - Reference corpus for confinement: the poured pages of the same $L value (as in S). N2 and N1 as specified, 200 draws each,
    q99 = sorted index 197.
  Arms: NAME (poured real chapters) and RARITY (before pouring, every name-stem token is replaced by 'et'; after pouring, the
  paragraph-initial token of line 1 is replaced by a fresh type found nowhere else).
  PASS = NAME fires (S > N2 q99) in >= 10/15 seeds AND RARITY fires in <= 5/15 seeds, failed seeds counted as above.
  Fixture result (made-up count list, 112 pages, 28 strata, 2 held in place): NAME 15/15, RARITY 0/15, PASS; count-list and own-hash
  mismatches exit 2; pages longer than nearly every chapter fail all 15 seeds -> NAME 0/15, RARITY 15/15, FAIL. FAIL stops s128 before any Voynich text
  is read. Any repeat of N2 known-answer checks after the read step is report-only and cannot change the call.

GATES AFTER THE VOYNICH READ, BEFORE THE REAL SCORE (real herbal pages, real sizes and layout, ZL3b whole words)
- G1b DECISIVE planted gate (the Egerton placement), seeds 20261101..20261115 (15). On each page, the paragraph-initial token of line 1 is
  replaced by a fresh type unique to that page; with probability 0.535 (Egerton start_N90 share of chapters whose name recurs >= 2,
  calibration file line 9, column 'recurs>=2') 1-3 (uniform) further copies replace random tokens of the same page outside line 1.
  PASS = planted S > planted-corpus N2 q99 (200 draws) in >= 10/15 seeds. FAIL -> CALL NOT_POWERED.
  Full-call power, REPORT-ONLY (changes neither G1b nor the call): per G1b seed the scorer also prints whether planted S >= 0.117 and
  whether the planted corpus is LOQO_MET (LOQO as below, on the planted pages, 200 draws per qualifying quire, drawn from the same
  seed's RNG stream after its G1b N2 draws, quires in the LOQO order), and the number of seeds out of 15 with all three of planted
  S > N2 q99, planted S >= 0.117 and planted LOQO_MET. If that number is < 10/15 it prints G1b_FULL_CALL_LOW beside the call.
- G1a planted gate, reported only, seeds 20261201..20261215 (15): as G1b, but the plant replaces a random non-paragraph-initial token of
  line 1. A page whose line 1 has only one token gets no G1a plant (left unplanted) and is counted; if such pages are > 10% of the
  pages of the s128 page set, G1a is printed as G1a_REDUCED.
- Macer-strength versions of G1b and G1a (recurrence probability 0.364, Macer start_N90 'recurs>=2', calibration file line 18),
  seeds 20261301..20261315 and 20261401..20261415: reported only.
- One-token line 1 in G1b: the plant still goes into the paragraph-initial slot (the line's only token); recurrence copies go outside
  line 1 as above. If a page has no included tokens outside line 1, it receives no recurrence copies; the count is printed.

LEAVE-ONE-QUIRE-OUT (no parameter is fitted; thresholds 2 and 0.9 are fixed from calibration)
- Qualifying quire: a herbal quire with >= 4 pages of the s128 page set. For each, S_q on its pages (confinement still against the full same-language
  reference corpus) and N2 restricted to that quire's strata, 200 draws. One RNG stream, seed 20261501, quires processed in ascending
  $Q order.
- LOQO_MET if at least 3 quires qualify and S_q > N2_q q95 in >= ceil(2/3 x qualifying quires); q95 = sorted draw index
  ceil(0.95 x draws) - 1 (189 at 200 draws).
- LOQO_NOT_MET if at least 3 quires qualify and fewer pass. LOQO_NOT_ASSESSABLE if fewer than 3 quires qualify.

CALL (ZL3b, whole words, pooled herbal). Rules are tested in this order; the first that applies is the call, so every outcome maps to
exactly one call.
0. (Reached only if F0, the count list (d0), F0-N2-REAL (d1) and the count-list rebuild (d) all passed; otherwise s128 stopped.)
1. If G1b failed: NOT_POWERED (S and the nulls are printed, not interpreted).
2. Else if S <= N1 q99: ABSENT.
3. Else if S <= N2 q99: RARITY_ONLY (here N1 q99 < S <= N2 q99).
4. Else (S > max(N1 q99, N2 q99)) if S >= 0.117 and LOQO_MET: NAME_SLOT_PRESENT.
5. Else (S > max(N1 q99, N2 q99) but S < 0.117, or LOQO_NOT_MET, or LOQO_NOT_ASSESSABLE): MIXED, printed with the failing condition(s).
- Floor 0.117: Macer start_N90 S (calibration file line 18), the weakest real named herbal at Voynich-like page size that beats its own
  null (p 0.01). The floor is set AT Macer's value so a Macer-strength name signal passes; it is not meant to exclude Macer-strength signals.

REPORTED, NOT CALLED
- N1 beside N2 (required). Herbal A and B separately. RF1b, IT2a, SlotSegmenter cores, Zattera cores: Benjamini-Hochberg at FDR 0.05
  on the N2 p-values across 12 cells = 4 variants (RF1b whole words, IT2a whole words, ZL3b SlotSegmenter cores, ZL3b Zattera cores)
  x 3 page groups (pooled herbal, Herbal A, Herbal B), report-only, seeds as for the primary nulls.
- Descriptive: for hit pages, median own-page count of the line-1 type, share that recur beyond line 1, median share of other
  same-language herbal pages containing the type (Egerton other-chapter fraction 0.0019 at start_N90, calibration file line 9).
- Stolfi first-token uniqueness rate with its N2 value, marked non-diagnostic (calibration CALL_D).

INTERPRETATION LIMITS (fixed now)
- NAME_SLOT_PRESENT locates where a plant-name crib should be tried (line 1, page-confined, self-recurring). It reads nothing, does not
  show the type is a plant name, and does not move the scoreboard until the Independent Verifier accepts it.
- RARITY_ONLY: the page-start signal is the known paragraph-initial vocabulary (L-069); page confinement gives "first word = plant name"
  no support. ABSENT: no page-start name signal at Egerton strength (the strength G1b checks power for); a weaker, Macer-strength
  signal (recurrence 0.364, power reported only) is not ruled out. MIXED: no claim either way.
- No re-run with changed thresholds, units, strata or seeds under s128; any change is a new run id, and a new run id never replaces
  a filed s128 result (FILING, under STATUS AND ORDER).

OUTPUTS
- Scorer (reserved): tools/s128_name_slot_score.py. Results: runs/s128/results_s128_name_slot_<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS>.txt, one file per run,
  never overwritten; CALL lines filed as printed.
